Title: Parked-cwd guard: realpath-normalize cwd to close the symlink-traversal bypass
Created: 2026-07-13
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-07-13T14:36Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context

Found by the review panel on PR #545 (ticket 0306) and confirmed pre-existing
since ticket 0267: in `scripts/guard-enterworktree-parked-cwd.sh`, the
`git check-ignore -q "$cwd"` call errors with "outside repository" when `$cwd`
reaches the repo through a symlink, and the guard treats the non-zero exit as
allow. A parked runtime directory addressed via a symlinked path therefore
bypasses the deny — on both guarded surfaces (EnterWorktree and, since #545,
Skill).

## Actions

1. Normalize `$cwd` with `realpath` (or `pwd -P` equivalent) before the
   repo-membership and check-ignore probes.
2. Add a symlink test case to `tests/test_guard_enterworktree_parked_cwd.sh`:
   a symlinked path into a git-ignored runtime dir is denied; a symlinked
   path to a legitimate repo root stays allowed. Red-first.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Symlinked parked cwd is denied on both surfaces
- [ ] Symlinked legitimate cwd stays allowed
- [ ] `make check` passes
